cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the associated research article and this software repository."
title: "Historical Universe Contamination in an Adaptive Trend-Following Backtest: Reproducibility Package"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Czarnecki
    given-names: Marek
affiliation: "Walsh College"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Marek-Czarnecki/return-predictability-australia"
url: "https://github.com/Marek-Czarnecki/return-predictability-australia"
abstract: "Public reproducibility package for a study showing, in a controlled same-vendor Australian adaptive trend-following experiment, that retrospective historical-universe construction materially changes measured benchmark-relative performance. Exact decomposition separates the distortion into direct universe-composition and endogenous parameter-selection channels, with aggregate concentration diagnostics assessing whether the composition effect is diffuse or survivor-dominated."
keywords:
  - historical universe contamination
  - point-in-time index membership
  - survivorship bias
  - trend following
  - Australian equities
  - walk-forward testing
  - parameter selection
  - reproducibility
